              "locked": false,
              "content": {
                "html": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Most patients feel completely well after their examination and can return to their normal daily activities unless advised otherwise by the Nuclear Medicine team.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">A small amount of radioactivity remains in your body for a short time after your scan. For some examinations you may be advised to:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Drink plenty of fluids to help remove the tracer more quickly.</span></p></li><li><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Minimise prolonged close contact with pregnant women, babies and young children for the remainder of the day.</span></p></li><li><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Follow any additional advice provided by your department.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">There is no need to avoid providing essential care to children or family members unless specifically advised.</span></p><p></p>",
                "colorRole": "default",
